{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**Anti-vacuity.**  A genuinely `q↔q⁻¹`-odd object exists (`g n = n`); it does\nhave zero constant coefficient, so `barAntisym_const_zero`'s hypothesis is\nsatisfiable and the headline distinction is real, not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.certified_offset_not_barAntisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.certified_offset_not_barAntisym","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**Headline (honest negative).**  No Laurent object whose constant coefficient\nequals the certified offset datum can be `q↔q⁻¹`-antisymmetric.  Hence the\ncertified saddle offset's `q = 1` vanishing is **not** delivered by the\nbar-fixed-point argument — the offset is a cross-chirality difference (constant\ncoefficient `1 ≠ 0`), not a genuinely bar-odd-in-`q` object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.offsetConst_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.offsetConst_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.offsetConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.offsetConst","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L99-L101","doc":"The certified `q → 0` constant coefficient of the 5₂ offset is the merged\ndistinguisher's ι-odd datum `chiralityOdd 4 3 = 1` (reused, not a fresh number). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_const_zero_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_const_zero_int","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L94-L97","doc":"**Bar-fixed-point vanishing over `ℤ`** (a domain — no `Invertible 2` needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.barAntisym_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L81-L92","doc":"**Bar-fixed-point vanishing (generic).**  A `q↔q⁻¹`-odd Laurent object has\nzero constant (degree-0) coefficient.  This is the mechanism that forces any\ngenuinely bar-odd object to vanish at the fixed point `q = q⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.BarAntisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SaddleOffsetBarGrade.BarAntisym","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SaddleOffsetBarGrade.lean#L76-L79","doc":"A Laurent-coefficient sequence `g : ℤ → R` is **q↔q⁻¹-antisymmetric**\n(bar-odd in the modulus): the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`, acting on coefficients by\n`n ↦ -n`, negates it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}